items.description:
The diff-quality proof item is still open and falls here: point a no-sync Application at an existing live release and check the live-vs-git diff reads sensibly, once on dev before staking the cutover on it. The slice supplies the manifest and procedure in `/work/Ansible/docs/runbooks/argocd.md`:
- a hand-made dev-stage Application with no automated sync and no cascade-delete finalizer;
- it carries the four `hook.*` parameters;
- it is named apart from the `kubecoder-dev` the registry will generate;
- it is never synced;
- its UI diff against the live release is reviewed, then it is deleted.
Applying and deleting it is recorded as the operator's outstanding action.
